{
  "headline": "Multi-agent systems deployed to production in days, not months — on Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres",
  "subheadline": "Every service we offer is built around one operational reality: multi-agent systems fail in production for architectural reasons, not capability reasons. Misconfigured Kafka consumer groups cause task duplication under load. Agents without pod-level isolation take down unrelated pipelines when they fault. No observability means no debugging when it matters. We build the infrastructure that handles these failure modes before they reach your production environment — and we do it on open standards you own outright."
}

{
  "headline": "Gripper Selection Tools Built for Specification Decisions",
