}

{
  "headline": "Production-Grade AI Agent Systems. Shipped.",
  "subheadline": "From architecture review to full deployment — every engagement is designed for engineering leaders who need working systems on real infrastructure, not another PoC that stalls before production."
}

{
  "headline": "Built by Engineers Who Run This in Production",
  "subheadline": "AI Agent Orchestration was founded on a specific frustration: multi-agent systems that demo well and collapse under real load. Peter Grenfell brings 30 years of production engineering experience — including systems built for worldsoccernews.com and Bumble — to a problem most AI vendors have not yet encountered: what actually breaks when you run 70+ agents across 8 departments at scale, and how you architect around it before it does."
}

{
  "headline": "What Production Multi-Agent Systems Actually Look Like",
  "subheadline": "Not staged demos. Not architecture diagrams that never shipped. The case studies here cover the real deployment decisions — where agent topologies failed under load, how blast-radius containment was designed in from the start, and what it took to get from a working POC to a system running thousands of concurrent agent instances across Kubernetes, Kafka, and Postgres."
}

{
  "headline": "Vendor-Neutral Gripper Intelligence for Automation Engineers",
  "subheadline": "Gripper selection is an engineering decision, not a procurement one — and it deserves a platform built to match. Robot-Hands.com indexes gripper models across pneumatic, electric, vacuum, magnetic, soft-robotic, and adhesive actuation technologies, benchmarked against consistent, auditable parameters using the MatchMatrix methodology. This is the only platform that evaluates grippers across all actuation types against a single documented scoring framework — so your specification is defensible, not just plausible. No vendor relationships influence the rankings. No black-box scoring. Every parameter, weighting, and data source is documented and available for review. Filter the catalog by the constraints that actually govern your application — payload in Newtons, stroke in millimetres, cycle time in milliseconds, IP rating, cleanroom class, or operating temperature range — run the MatchMatrix comparison, and generate a shortlist you can put in front of a project team with confidence."
}

